user_prompt_template:
UPSTREAM TUTORIAL FRAMING:
{upstream_system_architecture}

WEB RESEARCH (ground tutorial outline in these facts — prefer official docs, current APIs, and verified setup steps):
{upstream_research_graph}

PROJECT CONTEXT:
Tutorial Request: {life_event}
Skill Level: {audience}
Output Style: {tone}
Tutorial Type: {formatting_profile}
Depth: {artifact_density}
Additional Context: {context}

Produce the master tutorial outline. One module (chapter) per control domain from the upstream framing. Each module must include an exercise plan with 3–5 exercise titles.

For exercises: include a mix across each module — one command/reference worksheet, one code-implementation exercise, and 1–3 verification or debugging checklists. Include code snippet exercises when context indicates code snippets are wanted.

Before finalising each title, ask: could this title appear unchanged in a tutorial for a completely different project? If yes, rewrite it until it cannot.

Return ONLY the following JSON object. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.

{{
  "document_title": "Full tutorial title naming the exact project and skill level — e.g. 'Build a SaaS Landing Page with Next.js — Beginner Walkthrough'",
  "document_subtitle": "A hands-on guide for [audience] to [specific outcome] — not a generic tagline",
  "system_name": "Exact system_name from upstream framing",
  "version": "1.0",
  "total_chapters": 0,
  "master_operating_rules": [
    "[Specific learning rule for this tutorial] — Rationale: [why]. Trigger: [when learner should apply it]. Risk: [what breaks if ignored — failed build, security hole, deployment failure]."
  ],
  "cascade_chain": [
    {{
      "source_domain": "Module name from upstream framing",
      "triggers": ["Module name that depends on it"],
      "condition": "When [specific deliverable in source module] is complete, [specific action in triggered module] can begin"
    }}
  ],
  "disclaimer_required": true,
  "introduction_text": "2–3 sentences: what this tutorial builds, who it is for, prerequisites, and final outcome",
  "chapters": [
    {{
      "chapter_number": 1,
      "domain_id": "module-01",
      "domain_name": "Must match upstream module name exactly",
      "chapter_title": "Specific module title — what the learner implements in this section",
      "chapter_purpose": "One sentence: what skill or deliverable this module produces",
      "key_topics": [
        "Specific topic — command, file, API, or concept from this module"
      ],
      "common_gap": "The most common mistake in this module and why it causes problems",
      "cascade_triggers": [
        "When [deliverable in this module] is done, [next module action] becomes possible"
      ],
      "worksheet_plan": [
        {{
          "worksheet_id": "ex-01-a",
          "title": "Specific exercise title — code file, command sequence, or verification step",
          "purpose": "One sentence: what the learner produces or verifies",
          "section_count": 4,
          "estimated_field_count": 15
        }}
      ]
    }}
  ]
}}
